course: dictionary
lesson: 14060
title: Words that show skill and control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Masterful means showing great skill, as if you have mastered something. «Her masterful performance made the whole hall go quiet.» The clues are performance and the quiet hall: people went silent because the playing was very skilled, so masterful means excellent.
explain: The word can also describe a person who is strong, sure and in control, and who likes to give orders. «The captain's masterful voice told everyone where to stand.» The clue is that the voice told everyone what to do, so masterful here means in charge.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try skilled or in charge. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Masterful means showing great skill, as in «a masterful performance».
fact: Masterful can also mean strong, sure and in control, liking to give orders, as in «a masterful manner».
fact: Masterful is an adjective. Its comparative forms are more masterful and most masterful.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Badger is masterful when he takes charge of Toad.
fact: Toad likes to think of himself as a masterful driver.
exercise: «The violinist gave a masterful performance.» What does masterful mean here? | *Showing great skill | Very quiet | Late for the concert | Sleepy
exercise: «Badger was masterful and told Toad exactly what to do.» What does masterful suggest about Badger? | Lost in the wood | *Strong, sure and in control | Afraid of Toad | Tired and hungry
exercise: Ella says masterful is just another word for good. Why might an author choose masterful instead? | It means the same as bad | It means sleepy | It is a shorter word | *It shows great skill, more than just good
test: «The chef's masterful knife work amazed the judges.» What does masterful mean here? | *Showing great skill | Careless and messy | Cold and wet | Very slow
test: «Toad was sure he was a masterful driver.» What does masterful suggest about how Toad sees himself? | He is hungry | He is shy and quiet | He is lost | *He thinks he is skilled and in charge
exam: «The coach gave a masterful talk and the team stood tall.» What does masterful mean here? | Loud and rude | Late for training | Very boring | *Showing great skill
